d 'TWFEDEC': module to compute Two-way fixed effects coefficient as a weighted average of first-difference coefficients
d
d    twfedec decomposes the coefficient on a scalar treatment in a
d two-way fixed effects (TWFE) regression on a balanced panel,
d following Ishimaru (2026, The Econometrics Journal, Theorem 2.2).
d The TWFE coefficient equals a weighted average of k-period
d first-difference (FD) coefficients over all horizons k = 1, ...,
d T-1; with time-varying covariates, an adjustment term is added.
d twfedec reports the TWFE coefficient, the FD coefficients, the
d weights, and the adjustment term, and optionally plots the FD
d coefficients and weights by horizon. 
d
d KW: panel data
d KW: TWFE
d KW: fixed effects
d
d Requires: Stata version 15 and reghdfe, ftools from SSC (q.v.)
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260925
d
d Author:    Shoya Ishimaru,   Hitotsubashi University
d Support: email  shoya.ishimaru@@r.hit-u.ac.jp
d
f twfedec.ado
f twfedec.sthlp
f twfedec_example.dta
